{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Behold we perish, we are lost.</b> Some of them died their own death, and some of them were lost through judgment — that would suffice for us. But not only that, rather all of us are lost. How so? 'Everyone who approaches the mishkan of HaShem dies' — they supposed that 'the stranger who approaches shall be put to death' had not yet been said, but only regarding those with blemishes."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:25.169131217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}